 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:23:41 +0200

rust-proxmox-schema (5.4.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * oneOf: drop support for a plain string variant, added in 5.2.0. The
    variants of a oneOf schema and the members of an allOf schema must be
    object schemas, or allOf and oneOf schemas made of those. This is now
    checked at compile time, so schemas using a string variant no longer
    compile.

  * oneOf: reject at compile time a variant with a property of the same name
    as the type property, as the two would clash.

  * return `&'static Schema` from the lookup methods of schemas and of the
    `ObjectSchemaType` trait, as schemas are always static. A looked-up
    schema can now be kept without borrowing the schema it came from.

  * multi-line comments: check the whole value for control characters. The
    pattern accepted any value with one line free of them, which includes
    every value ending in a newline. Newlines and tabs stay allowed. A stored
    comment with any other control character, for example in a Proxmox
    Backup Server node description, must be edited before its configuration
    can be saved again.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:40:58 +0200

rust-proxmox-schema (5.3.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * add support for declaring deprecated property aliases on object schemas,
    so a renamed property keeps accepting its old name while the schema and
    generated documentation advertise only the new one. Aliases are honored
    by the CLI, property-string and query/form parsing, and can be rewritten
    to the canonical name for JSON request bodies.

